---
title: "check-superset diagnostics"
---

This document deliberately trips every static superset validator that reports a defect
you cannot see in the rendered page. It lives in `corpus/diagnostics/`, which is exempt
from the corpus clean-render guards.

**It must stay free of code cells.** `diagnostics/anchors.rs` conservatively switches the
manual-anchor check off for any document that executes, because a cell can mint an id at
runtime (`HTML('<div id="x">')`), so adding one cell here would silently retire the
duplicate-id and broken-jump halves of this fixture with every gate still green.

## Heading {#dup}

First section.

## Another {#dup}

A second heading reusing the same explicit id (duplicate DOM id).

A [broken in-page jump](#no-such-anchor) that lands nowhere, and a missing image:
![alt text](no-such-image.png).

Cited [@ghost2020] with no `bibliography:` declared, so the reference renders as a raw key.

Two families that used to be pinned here went on 2026-08-08: a malformed `$\frac{$`
(KaTeX renders it as a red error span, so the author can see it) and a typo'd fence
language (` ```pyton ` renders unhighlighted, which is visible too). What stays is the
set nothing in the page reveals.
